## Evaluation and limitations

The eight disjoint public-regression cases were visible before training.
Their twelve exact counts are a contamination-prone regression vector, not a
sealed or generalization result and not a scalar rank. The base is a tiny,
primarily English model and may be inaccurate, brittle, biased, or produce
text outside the six intended labels. Generated behavior cannot establish an
inner state or enforce rights, permission, authority, withdrawal, or safety.
New `agenttool-revocable-feedback-model-scorecard/0.2` records distinguish an
applicable metric with zero counted observations from an inapplicable metric
with a zero denominator. The frozen first public `/0.1` scorecard predates those
denominators, so its zero counts alone do not establish metric applicability.

